# Exercise the API from VS Code (REST Client extension: click "Send Request").
# Start the API first: `make api` (local mode, in-memory).

@host = http://localhost:8000
@api = {{host}}/api/v1

### Health
GET {{host}}/health

### Artisan: create a listing (returns an UploadTicket)
# @name create
POST {{api}}/products
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Hand-thrown clay mug",
  "description": "Wheel-thrown and glazed by hand.",
  "price": 450,
  "tags": ["pottery", "kitchen"],
  "artisan_name": "Meera"
}

### What the app checks before uploading (15-min cap, file types, chunk size)
GET {{api}}/upload-policy

### Local mode: "upload" the video to the fake resumable target (marks it ready)
PUT {{create.response.body.upload_url}}
Content-Range: bytes 0-4/5

hello

### Tags for the filter chips
GET {{api}}/tags

### Buyer: search by keyword
GET {{api}}/products?q=clay

### Buyer: filter by tag, 10 per page
GET {{api}}/products?tag=pottery&limit=10

### Buyer: product details
GET {{api}}/products/{{create.response.body.product.id}}

### Buyer: place an order
POST {{api}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "product_id": "{{create.response.body.product.id}}",
  "buyer_name": "Ravi",
  "quantity": 2
}
